Chapter: X86-64 Boot Infrastructure
  cites Codex chapter Numbers
  cites Codex chapter Lists

 Bare-metal boot sequence, interrupt handling, process management,
 syscall dispatch, and capability model.

Section: Memory Address Map

 Sorted by address. To add a new entry, find the gap and confirm
 the preceding allocation has ended.

 LOAD-BEARING CONSTANTS — every value in this section is compiled
 into the seed as a hardcoded x86-64 immediate (via `li`, `cmp-ri`,
 `add-ri` in emit functions). Changing any value here WITHOUT a seed
 rebuild causes the old seed to silently emit code with the old values.
 The new values only take effect after `build/build.ps1` produces a
 new fixed-point seed.

 The same applies to constants in "Size and Threshold Constants" and
 "BuildSettings.codex" that are used in emit functions. When in doubt,
 rebuild the seed.

 `build/build.ps1` checks a hash of these constants against
 `seed/constants.hash` and warns if they differ.

